<title>SINGAPORE: Lee Kim 1996 net down 52 pct to S$2.4 mln.</title>
<headline>Lee Kim 1996 net down 52 pct to S$2.4 mln.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>		   (in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			     2.37  vs    4.89</p>
<p>    Dividend (percent)		   7.00  vs    8.00</p>
<p>    Group shr (cents)		    2.94  vs    6.16</p>
<p>    Group shr (fuly diluted)	   2.67  vs    5.05</p>
<p>    Turnover				29.78  vs  360.12</p>
<p>    Other income incl. interest	2.16  vs    0.91</p>
<p>    Interest (expense)		   3.44  vs    1.19</p>
<p>    Depreciation (expense)	     0.32  vs    0.77</p>
<p>    Profits from associates	    0.04  vs    2.15</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			 4.10  vs    5.97</p>
<p>    Tax					1.69  vs    3.24</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries	     (gain) 0.57  vs    4.25 (gain)</p>
<p>Dividend pay date: July 15, 1997</p>
<p>Last day books open: July 4, 1997</p>
<p>Note - Lee Kim Tah Holdings Ltd is a property development company.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
</text>
